{
  "explanation": "The attacker from IP 45.33.32.156 attempted multiple Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks by injecting malicious JavaScript payloads into HTTP GET parameters such as '/search', '/profile', and '/redirect'. The payloads were designed to steal sensitive user data like session cookies and execute arbitrary scripts in the context of the victim's browser session. Based on the logs, the application successfully blocked or returned HTTP 400/302 responses, indicating that the attempts likely failed or were intercepted.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Initial Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Implement context-aware output encoding for all user-supplied data before rendering it in the DOM.",
    "Deploy a robust Content Security Policy (CSP) to restrict the execution of inline scripts and unauthorized external domains.",
    "Validate and sanitize all incoming request parameters on the server-side to reject payloads containing HTML or JavaScript tags."
  ]
}
